          'What is MCP? Which servers are active (`storybook-<framework>`, `nx-mcp`, `figma-console`, `uianatomy`)?',
          'Toolset model (since Storybook 10.4, the repo runs 10.6.0): docs / dev / test — hosted vs. local surface, including toolset gating (when `test` is disabled for read-only agents)',
          'Live exercise: ask Claude for Button props, print token values, preview in chat',
          'Negative demo: the same question in a browser chat without MCP → hallucination. With MCP → correct answer',
          'Write one story with a `play` function for a variant, watch it fail, fix it, watch it pass',
        ],
        stretch:
          "Ask the MCP server for a prop that does not exist and read how it answers. Then say why 'not documented' is the right answer.",
        recap: 'Why is a story a claim, and who checks that the claim holds?',
        trainer: [
          'Storybook 10.6 background for questions: `npx storybook tools` / `npx storybook skills` is the route for agents without an MCP client (`storybook ai` is deprecated); `experimentalDocgenServer` is set explicitly for Angular and Vue; CSF Factories become the default story format in Storybook 11 and the workshop deliberately still writes CSF3.',
        ],
      },
      {
        num: '05',
        time: '16:10–17:15 · 65 min',
        title: 'Kata against the clock',
        format: 'Hands-on, no guidance',
        why: 'Repeat the loop without guidance.',
        pages: [L.firstComponent, L.findingCodes],
        done: 'The kata is green and every parity finding is labelled.',
        bullets: [
          `The 15-minute /first-component kata: the same ${TARGET.name} frame (node ${TARGET.node}) as a second round against the clock, seven copy-paste steps, with the same \`figma_check_design_parity\` at the end`,
          'The component lives under `workshop-<fw>/src/` and is viewed in your own app with `nx serve workshop-<fw>` — step 4 of the kata page says so',
          'Label every parity finding: code, Figma, or contract',
        ],
        stretch:
          'Write the handoff document for the kata frame before you prompt, and compare the result with the first round.',
