          'All participants, whatever the framework: start `npm run storybook` in parallel, then connect with `claude mcp add --transport http storybook-local http://localhost:<port>/mcp` (use the port Storybook prints) — deliberately local scope (the default of `--scope`, not project): the shared `.mcp.json` stays untouched and the working tree clean. Reconnect the client and check that the dev/test tools (`get-storybook-story-instructions`, `stories-preview`, `test-run`) are now listed — identical for all three frameworks since 10.6.0. Without this step the required tool that follows simply does not exist: "not available" here means "not configured", not "server down". `get-storybook-story-instructions` is mandatory before every `*.stories.*` edit',
          'The prompt comes from the handoff document of Block 01, not from the picture alone — behaviour and exclusions from the document, not just the look. Let Claude produce the contract (typed through the `ComponentContract` schema from `workshop-<fw>/src/contracts/types.ts`, imported relatively), the component (including its test) and the stories in one step: one story per variant value and Boolean state, with a `play` for every behaviour line of the document. One step, not three — the stories import the component and do not compile without it; the `atelier-component` skill treats it as one step anyway',
          'LLM-friendly API rules: predictable naming, literal unions, composition over config, no hidden defaults',
